// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2514684212" "Excellent work as usual, {HeroName}, although I'm beginning to get worried. The Council definitely has a bigger picture planned, one that we're not fully aware of. I don't believe Calvin Scott is aware of it... or if he is, perhaps he's somehow going along with it.<br><br>Alec Parson and I will continue to do more work investigating what the Council could be planning. Pendragon and Aurora are working on fighting Archon Burkholder in Striga Isle, although it appears that the Council and UPA have formed a much tighter defense on the island than we previously expected. We also believe  that <color yellow>Marauder has his abilities back</color>, judging by some of the small craters we've seen on the island. This calls for drastic measures, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Grant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3998243124" "<color orange>Grant Creston looks like he's been badly injured. Whoever did this wanted him alive to send a message to you. Grant wheezes painfully.</color><br><br>There... never was... a meeting. It was a trick... by <color yellow>Arakhn</color>... she wants to show that... the Council will win... no matter what... that they will always be... a step ahead... of us. Y-you have to stop her... {HeroName}.<br><br>Don't be... intimidated... by her... or these... Nictus freaks...<br><br>I can... I can help... I can still get up and... do something..."
// Answer Text :
"P2468781446" "You've done enough, Grant. (Activate Grant's medi-porter)"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2425303094" "You've been doing excellent work, {HeroName}, but we're still behind in this war against the Council. Every victory we get causes them to fortify their position in Striga Isle. I'm speaking with a man named Admiral Sutter about the situation.<br><br>Grant Creston was contacted by Positron about uniting the Vindicators and Freedom Phalanx in an attack on Striga Isle. He should be meeting with the groups at any minute now.<br><br>We need you to attend the meeting as the official representative of the New Praetorians. After that, Grant will continue his investigations regarding Arakhn."
// AcceptString :
"P865759282" "Everyone working together? Sounds like a plan."
// SendOffString :
"P176190310" "Exactly. You'll be leading the charge once we get everything settled. Both groups still have their hands full, of course, but we must try to convince them that this is the <i>only</i> way we're going to win this war against the Council.<br><br>I'll give you the location where Grant is meeting with the others. They may not listen to him, but I'm sure they'll listen to what you have to say on the matter."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2252538661" "Meet with the Paragon Supergroups"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3201572754" "<color orange>Provost Marchand's line is busy.</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3731517584" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Call to Action</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P950776687" "Something definitely isn't right. The Council is here! Have they attacked the Phalanx and the Vindicators?"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - OnEnterObjectiveComplete 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3325282445" "Find Grant Creston"
// Script Variable WaypointNames :
"P1982635759" "Grant Creston"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - ObjectiveTrigger 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2525949873" "Have you heard the rumors? The disturbances?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1387135556" "<t=2 d=2><t=5 d=5>I have. Requiem is on the move. We focus on Arakhn and the Center, first."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4089913483" "The Praetorian put up a surprising fight."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P635403138" "<t=2 d=2><t=5 d=5>He couldn't defeat Arakhn in the end, even with all his skills."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4013135737" "What about Nosferatu and Maestro?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P480077648" "<t=2 d=2><t=5 d=5>Arakhn is tasked with freeing them after she kills the heroes."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3656129885" "Why are Burkholder and Vandal allowed to stay in the main base?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P413339662" "<t=2 d=2><t=5 d=5>They're working on the War Walkers. We're in full production now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// CutScene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// 5 Actor2 :
"P2202844704" "<em frustrated t=5 d=5>I told you, Requiem, I am the only leader of the Nictus. You wish to argue that?"
// 5 Actor1 :
"P362807910" "<em no t=5 d=5>I'm merely giving you a chance, Arakhn. The 5th Column is rising."
// 5 Actor1 :
"P624492745" "<em thanks t=5 d=5>Join myself and the Reichsman and you will keep control over your Nictus."
// 5 Actor2 :
"P1639503853" "<em disagree t= 5 d=5>Pah! Once the Center's plans are finished, the Nictus will be stronger than ever!"
// 5 Actor1 :
"P1678208730" "<em shrug t=5 d=5>... Hah. We'll see how you fare against {HeroName}, then. Good day, Arakhn."
// Script Variable ACTOR_1_NAME :
"P2026798565" "Requiem"
// Script Variable ACTOR_2_NAME :
"P1514724335" "Arakhn"
// Script Variable ACTOR_3_NAME :
"P534853849" "NAME"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P337629768" "Give me a hand here, {HeroName}, she won't go quietly!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3731237859" "Alright {HeroName}, we can clean this up if we kill Washington!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1652439080" "You couldn't stop us, {HeroName}! The Shadow Seed was one of many plans. I'll make sure you don't live to see the others!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3184784374" "You can't stop the Council now, {HeroName}. The Center's glorious plans will come to light, and you... you will serve well as a Nictus host!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Arakhn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3029373105" "Defeat Arakhn"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2984520259" "You defeated Arakhn!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4281012919" "You defeated Arakhn and discovered more of the Council's true plans!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3153842040" "Grant is recovering in Brickstown's hospital. He put up a damn good fight against Arakhn.<br><br>We were fooled by them, {HeroName}. They wanted to split us apart. They were just using the attacks on Founders' Falls and Croatoa to test their toys, and we showed them that they needed to do better.<br><br>The Phalanx and Vindicators are still busy dealing with other threats in both Paragon and around the world. It's up to us to finish this, and we <i>are</i> going to finish it. We're done chasing around the Council wherever they pop up, {HeroName}. No more tests, no more doing things the safe way."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskOwnerIntro Text :
"P3891695810" "Alright, {HeroName}, we're here. Alec Parson is starting the teleporter now. You and the others will be taken past the walls.<br><br>Sutter has his naval ship outside of their firing range; they have enough turrets and War Walkers that they could blow us out of the water. Are you ready to go in with the others?"
// Page TaskOwnerIntro SayOutLoudText :
"P4059629848" "Alright, {HeroName}, we're here. Alec Parson is starting the teleporter now. You and the others will be taken past the walls."
// Answer Text :
"P164722086" "I'm ready, let's go."
// Answer Text :
"P1579877520" "Tell the others to stay and defend the ship. I'll go it alone."
// Page NotTaskOwnerIntroBegin Text :
"P576745064" "I need to speak to your team leader, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Page Teleport Text :
"P364314733" "<color yellow>Walk over to the teleporter nearby and you'll be taken to the Striga Island base.</color> We've got medical supplies set up to support you here, but just be aware that this ship could be attacked at any minute."
// Page Teleport SayOutLoudText :
"P2097701352" "Walk over to the teleporter nearby and you'll be taken to the Striga Island base."
// Answer Text :
"P156273299" "I'll keep that in mind, Marchand."
// Page HandleThings Text :
"P203104203" "Are you sure, {HeroName}? We could use the support, yes, but you're putting yourself in extreme danger by going after the Council by yourself.<br><br><color orange>The difficulty of the next part of the mission is extremely high. It is not advised to do the following alone and without any support from NPC allies or other players.</color>"
// Page HandleThings SayOutLoudText :
"P170778661" "Are you sure you want to go alone, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P3353777258" "On second thought, I'll take the help."
// Answer Text :
"P3744996055" "This has to be done, Marchand. Start the teleporter."
// Page TeleportWithout Text :
"P1205807426" "... Alright, {HeroName}. <color yellow>Walk over to the teleporter nearby and you'll be taken to the Striga Island base.</color>"
// Page TeleportWithout SayOutLoudText :
"P3743493832" "... Alright, {HeroName}. Walk over to the teleporter nearby and you'll be taken to the Striga Island base."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marauder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2574605640" "{HeroName}, hold your horses. Calvin Scott's gone in full retreat after he saw me comin' after him.<br><br>I used those Council fools to get my powers back. I know, the whole traitor deal, but I saw how you moved, you didn't need me 'round for this part. Someone had to get on the inside, and those idiots figured I'd be desperate enough to act like a spoiled dog.<br><br>I woulda tried to take 'em all on by myself, but there's way too many in that volcano base for me to handle. I figured I'd make my move now to get outta there and meet up with you and the others. You ready to do this?"
// Page Intro SayOutLoudText :
"P1617439637" "Hold your horses. I got myself into the Council to help the New Praetorians. I got my powers back, and now we can go after them together."
// Answer Text :
"P871996122" "How do I know I can trust you?"
// Page AmbushPage Text :
"P3447255354" "This world is full of super villains. They want to do evil things like take over the world."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Soldier 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P431297152" "We're all here from various divisions of the military. What we all have in common is loyalty and friendship to Admiral Sutter.<br><br>We all jumped at the chance to man this ship to help you in the attack on Striga, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}.<br><br>We'll move in once you establish the front. We all know you can do this, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}."
// Answer Text :
"P654442257" "Thanks for the support."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Sutter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page SutterTF Text :
"P3241278000" "<color orange>Admiral Sutter grins.</color><br><br>When Provost Marchand asked me for support in attacking Striga Isle, I knew it had to be backing you, {HeroName}. I still think of our time working together to fight off the Praetorian invasion.<br><br>I've spoken with the man called Riptide, the one who was at the forefront of the invasion. I don't harbor any ill will towards him. He's not a zealot, not like some of the others. He's a soldier, plain and simple.<br><br>I've gone on long enough, however. You don't have time to talk to this veteran, {HeroName}. There's an island of fascists out there that need a good punch to the face."
// Answer Text :
"P3948783435" "Thanks, Admiral, I'll handle it from here."
// Page Regular Text :
"P2378858336" "Good to see you, {HeroName}. My name is Admiral Sutter. I was able to call in a few favors to get the manpower to bring this ship out to sea. We're all here to give you support. In the event that you should fall, these men are going to do their best to storm that beach and take on the Council.<br><br>They're all willing to give their lives for this country, but I know it won't come to that. I know that you've got what it takes to take down these maniacs and show them that we don't tolerate their kind in this country.<br><br>I've gone on long enough, however. You don't have time to talk to this veteran, {HeroName}. There's an island of fascists out there that need a good punch to the face."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Parson 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P989183161" "Good luck out there! Sorry that I can't make it, but I need to handle the teleporter here. I kind of set it up at the very last minute, but I promise it'll work!<br><br>I've ran tests on some of the clockwork I built to make sure. Oh, you should've seen the initial results! One of them was teleported into a wall, and the other appeared on the ocean floor!<br><br>I'm just happy no one saw that... but I promise you have nothing to worry about, it's 100% working now!"
// Answer Text :
"P3514462294" "..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3118838989" "The Center and Calvin Scott think they have everything set to go for their invasion of America. Calvin Scott's army believes they have the know-how to defeat the soldiers of Primal Earth, while the Council has their parade of monstrosities. The Center is betting that we're too <i>scared</i> to try to attack them head-on. I lost the last gamble against him – I won't lose this one. We're going to prove him wrong, {HeroName}.<br><br>The time for caution is over. We're going to attack the Council's volcano base in Striga Isle head-on. Pendragon and Aurora report that the base's defenses are astronomical compared to earlier reports. They're getting <i>something</i> ready in there, {HeroName}, and we're going to stop it. I need to warn you, however, about one thing..."
// AcceptString :
"P3733956995" "What is it?"
// SendOffString :
"P395222094" "<color yellow>This could very well be a suicide mission.</color> The New Praetorians are down one man. At most, it's going to be yourself, Pendragon, Riptide, and Aurora against the Council's army. They'll have War Walkers, Vampryi, and Nictus waiting to destroy you.<br><br>By all accounts, we should not win this battle. However, I know you, {HeroName}. I know that if there's anyone who can pull through with this, it would be you.<br><br>Admiral Sutter has agreed to help us out. He and his men are going to take their vessel and bring us straight to Striga Isle. From there, Alec Parson will manage a teleportation system to get you past their walls and into the heart of the Council territory.<br><br>I don't know what you'll find in there, {HeroName}, or what your goal should be. All I can tell you is this: <color red>give them Hell.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3682894911" "Assault Striga Isle"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2533401772" "<color orange>Marchand's line has been turned off.</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2807296465" "<color deepskyblue>Part Four: Praetoria's Fury</color>"

